{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>See, I have begun, etc.</b> He said <b>הַחִלֹּתִי</b> in the past tense, referring back to the statement ״HaShem hardened his spirit in order to deliver him into your hand,״ and the statement <b>הַחִלֹּתִי</b> refers to the giving, not to the statement ״לְפָנֶיךָ.״ And Moses understood that it refers to everything stated, and therefore he pleaded before HaShem, thinking that the vow had been released, as they said of blessed memory (Sifrei, beginning of parashat Va'etchanan)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:33.051342489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}